SUMMARY:Crock of Pequannock Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this next hike in our Passaic Watershed series\, this time con
 tinuing up the Pequannock and Ramapo Rivers from where we last left off in
  Pompton Plains!\nWe'll meet at 9 am at Plaza 23\, which has the Stop and 
 Shop and Buy Rite Liquors closer to Jackson Avenue.\nThis is a 15 mile loo
 p\, so we'll begin right there\, and make our way along Jackson to the for
 mer Morris Canal crossing. If anyone wants to go and see the old Pompton L
 ock\, many can do this and hike through while I'll head with the stroller 
 on parallel roads out and around Riverview Farm.\nWe will follow several p
 leasant back roads and streets to the north\, visit the historic Schuyler-
 Colfax House\, and see the Pompton Lake Dam.\nFrom there we will had south
  on more of the Morris Canal Greenway\, which was where it followed the sl
 ackwater of the river.\nWe'll pass through Mathes Avenue Woodlands\, and s
 everal other properties to Ventimiglia tracts\, then to Willow Field.\nWe 
 get back on street a short bit\, then back to Hershfield Park where we'll 
 do a little loop.\nWe'll make our way toward Pompton Junction before turni
 ng back tracing the former Greenwood Lake Branch of the Erie Railroad agai
 n.\nMost of this is active\, so we'll be on closely parallel stuff on this
  part.\nToward the end\, it becomes the rail trail again which we'll follo
 w to where we left off\, then back to the plaza to close the loop.\nIf nee
 ded\, contact me at 908 343 8374
